{"content":[{"c":["ELIASAPH"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Leader of Gad’s tribe appointed by Moses. He was the son of Deuel (Reuel) (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.14","r":"Num.1.14","rawR":"Num.1.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.14","value":"Num.1.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.14","r":"Num.2.14","rawR":"Num.2.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.14","value":"Num.2.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.42,47","r":"Num.7.42,47","rawR":"Num.7.42,47","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.42,47","value":"Num.7.42,47"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:42, 47"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.20","r":"Num.10.20","rawR":"Num.10.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.20","value":"Num.10.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Gershonite Levite and the son of Lael. His responsibility in the tribe was to take charge of the tabernacle coverings, the curtains of the court and of the main altar (",{"href":"?bref=Num.3.24-25","r":"Num.3.24-25","rawR":"Num.3.24-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.3.24-25","value":"Num.3.24-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 3:24-25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eliasaph","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 1:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.14"},{"anchorText":"2:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.14","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.14","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.14"},{"anchorText":"7:42, 47","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.7.42,47","rawQueryValue":"Num.7.42,47","sourceRefExact":"Num.7.42,47"},{"anchorText":"10:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.20","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.20","sourceRefExact